  "title": "The knot is the only three-place law with mutual selection",
  "subject": "Whether any law besides not-all-equal has failing cubic systems that are recognisable and select it back",
  "conclusion": "Unless NP-complete problems are polynomial, not-all-equal is the only three-place knot whose failing cubic systems are non-empty and recognisable while its count is hard in general; parity is affine, the clause never fails, and the two pinning knots have coNP-complete failures. On plain systems, unconditionally, not-all-equal is the only knot that can fail.",
